<p>You can analyze <strong>all the remaining papers at once</strong> as long as you know their links.</p>
<pre><code>Analyze the remaining papers too and save them to files.</code></pre>
<p>Claude Code <strong>spawns several agents in parallel</strong> (for example 12 papers across 5–6 agents) and analyzes them at the same time. <strong>This is something a web chat cannot do.</strong> You can also turn the analysis results into <strong>detail pages</strong> for the paper showcase site you built earlier and link them up.</p>

<div class="note">
    <span class="nh">Another reason to use agents — saving context</span>
    An agent uses a <strong>separate context window</strong> from the main session. If you hand heavy analysis to an agent and take back only the result, you barely consume the main session's context, so quality holds up far longer. (See the next document.)
</div>
